data.content:
In .NET 10, `Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi` upgraded its dependency from **Microsoft.OpenApi v1.x to v2.x**. Here are the key breaking changes and fixes:

## Summary of Changes

| .NET 9 (OpenApi v1) | .NET 10 (OpenApi v2) |
|---|---|
| `OpenApiString`, `OpenApiInteger`, etc. | `JsonNode` (from `System.Text.Json.Nodes`) |
| `schema.Nullable = true/false` | `schema.Type` includes/excludes `JsonSchemaType.Null` |
| `new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "..." }` | `new OpenApiReference("oauth2")` (simplified) |
| `OpenApiSecurityRequirement` inherits `Dictionary<OpenApiSecurityScheme, IList<string>>` | Uses `.Schemes` dictionary property |

## Fixed Code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        // Example is now a JsonNode, not IOpenApiAny
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    // OpenApiReference is simplified; no more ReferenceType enum
    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
    {
        Reference = new OpenApiReference("oauth2")
    };

    // OpenApiSecurityRequirement no longer inherits from Dictionary;
    // use the .Schemes property instead
    var requirement = new OpenApiSecurityRequirement();
    requirement.Schemes.Add(oAuthScheme, scopes);
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement> { requirement };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
            {
                // Nullable bool is gone; remove "null" from the Type flags
                property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
            }
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

## Key Takeaways

1. **`Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` namespace is gone** — replace all `OpenApiString`/`OpenApiInteger`/etc. with `System.Text.Json.Nodes.JsonValue.Create(...)`.
2. **`Nullable` property removed** — nullable is now expressed via `JsonSchemaType.Null` in the `Type` flags enum.
3. **`OpenApiReference` simplified** — constructor takes the reference ID directly; the type is inferred from context.
4. **`OpenApiSecurityRequirement`** — no longer a dictionary itself; use its `.Schemes` property.
